media-gpu-route (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Nothing changes GPU without telling (Daniel, 2026-11-01; ORDER 346a,
    row U25): a caller that copies its pictures back decodes on the GPU the
    Graphics page names for players; a video that GPU cannot decode in
    hardware is decoded on another GPU that can, and that is said (the
    page's Decode on another GPU, on by default; [Decoding] OtherGpu,
    MEDIA_GPU_ROUTE_OTHER_GPU); turned off, it is decoded in software, and
    that is said. A page that fails, answers nothing or
    names a GPU this program cannot open, and a GPU whose decoder driver
    does not answer, are said in the person's language and nothing decodes
    on another GPU in their place.
  * media_gpu_route_decoder_said returns that reason and -2 when the GPU
    chosen for players cannot be resolved; the 0.2 entry points, which MLT
    and VLC call, answer software then and write the reason to stderr
    (their -1 sent them to the default GPU). The page is asked at each
    choice, no longer once per process, and its own stderr is kept.
  * media_gpu_route_copy_back_off_text: what a player says when it decodes
    in software because a conversion needs the pictures in memory and
    copying back is off (mpv's 3D conversion).
  * Messages in the edition's nine languages, chosen from the environment.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0300

